==Procedure==
# Mix ½ cup water, yeast, and sugar. Let it sit for 10 minutes until foamy.
# Place flour in a mixing bowl and sprinkle in the salt. Make a well, then add oil and yeast mixture. Stir in add small amounts of the remaining water until it forms a soft [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]] that can be moulded. Knead for 5 mins. Cover with paper and let rise for 1½ hours.
# Mix together the egg yolk and 1 tablespoon of water to make egg wash. Set aside.
# Divide dough into eight parts and roll each into a ball. Roll each bread into an oval shape 20 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]] long and 5 cm thick.
# Make lines in top of dough. [[Cookbook:Brush|Brush]] on egg wash, and sprinkle with black cumin seeds.
# Bake in a preheated 350°F (175°C) oven for 25 mins. Total cooking time is around 2½ hours.

